// The Ring 1 map update methods `set`/`remove` (value semantics: each returns a NEW map, the
// receiver is unchanged). `set` adds or overwrites a key; `remove` drops one (a no-op if absent).
// An aliased snapshot taken before an update is never mutated by it. Both backends agree.
// expect: stdout "[\"a\", \"b\"]"
// expect: stdout "[1, 9]"
// expect: stdout "[\"a\"]"
// expect: stdout "[\"a\", \"b\"]"
// expect: exit 0
mut m = { "a": 1 };
m = m.set("b", 2);
seen = m;
m = m.set("b", 9);
echo m.keys();
echo m.values();
m = m.remove("b");
echo m.keys();
echo seen.keys();
